# Burxt source. LF everywhere, so a checkout on Windows still compiles.
*.bx text eol=lf

# The specs and design notes are documentation, not the language's code. Marked
# so GitHub's language statistics describe the compiler rather than the prose.
DESIGN.md      linguist-documentation
README.md      linguist-documentation
spec/**        linguist-documentation

# The editor grammar is hand-written, not generated — GitHub's heuristics would
# otherwise be tempted to treat a large JSON file as vendored.
editors/vscode/syntaxes/*.json linguist-vendored=false

# NOTE on GitHub language detection: Burxt is not yet in github/linguist, so
# `.bx` files show as plain text on github.com. That is a popularity gate — 2000
# non-fork `.bx` files indexed in the last year, and Linguist filters out the
# primary language owner, so this repository's own files count for zero — not a
# technical one; the grammar Linguist requires already lives in
# editors/vscode/syntaxes/burxt.tmLanguage.json. Deliberately NOT worked around
# by mislabelling `.bx` as another language: a wrong label is worse than no
# label. See editors/README.md for the submission checklist.
